    "created_at": "2022-08-17T05:45:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-17T05:45:26Z",
    "body": "The \"universality\" in URIs does not uniqueness in correspondance, either from the reference to the referred object or the converse.  `file:///etc/passwd` is universal, even if the same reference refers to different objects.  And it is very common to see multiple references (or aliases) for the same resource on the web.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
