    "created_at": "2022-08-20T01:50:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-20T01:50:02Z",
    "body": "I'm not well-versed in this debate so bear with me here, but my intuition is that \"URI\" implies it can be used to fetch the resource, which is not the case here. The browser provides the identifier, but after that it's only useful as a tool for the developer to structure their databases.\r\n\r\nIf we planned to expose a `getHandleFrom{Id|Uri}()` method, then I agree that \"URI\" might be the right term. But that's explicitly a non-goal of this proposal...",
